4. Give Azure RBAC access for log storage
If you want your Azure identity to write Playwright logs to a storage account, run the following in PowerShell:

$storageId = az storage account show --name pwstrgrrdcac7 --resource-group RRD --query id -o tsv
az role assignment create --assignee "2e2def96-8717-40a0-8e01-c591673c64fb" --role "Storage Blob Data Contributor" --scope $storageId

This grants the specified principal permission to upload blobs to the storage account used for logs.
